# (Not the LOD.) A flat triangle (PRIM colour, 1-cycle) 10 rows high whose right edge is at x = 2100: the console's
# edges are 12 bits of whole pixels (28 bits in all), and one past 2047 wraps; the oracle draws none of these rows, the
# model draws 10..319. test_lod.c's floor has such rows (229 to 239).
rdram zero
cmd 3f10013f 00100000
cmd 2d000000 005003c0
cmd 2f000cf0 00000000
cmd 3a000000 ff8040ff
cmd 3cffffff fffff8db
cmd 08800078 00780050 08340000 00000000 000a0000 00000000 08340000 00000000
cmd 29000000 00000000
